<title>SWEDEN: SAS '96 pre-tax profit falls 31 pct.</title>
<headline>SAS '96 pre-tax profit falls 31 pct.</headline>
<dateline>STOCKHOLM 1997-02-17</dateline>
<text>
<p>SAS earnings for the 12 months to Dec 31 1996.</p>
<p>		    (millions of Swedish crowns unless stated)</p>
<p> Group pre-tax result		  1,815  vs   2,632</p>
<p> Group operating revenue	    35,189  vs  35,403</p>
<p> Operating costs			31,521  vs  30,641</p>
<p> Operating profit pre deprec	 3,668  vs   4,762</p>
<p> Depreciation			    1,851  vs   1,840</p>
<p> Associate interests	     CHARGE 15  vs	72 CREDIT</p>
<p> Operating profit after deprec     1,802  vs   2,994</p>
<p> Net financial items	    CHARGE 135  vs     300 CHARGE</p>
<p> Exchange rate difference	CREDIT 50  vs     151 CHARGE</p>
<p> Profit after fin items		1,717  vs   2,543</p>
<p> Minorities			   CHARGE 2  vs	 2 CHARGE</p>
<p>NOTE -- Full name of carrier is Scandinavian Airlines System, which is owned jointly by the governments of Sweden, Norway and Denmark and private investors.</p>
<p>SAS had forecast a 1996 pre-tax profit of 1.74 billion in the middle of November.</p>
<p>A poll of 10 analysts predicted full-year pre-tax profits of 1.72 billion crowns with forecasts ranging from 1.67 to 1.77 billion crowns.</p>
<p>-- Stockholm newsroom +46-8-700 1017</p>
</text>
